# Generating self-links from a class
#
# A reflexive property is associated with the class Human. N3 rules
# generate a backward definition that gives each member of that class a
# self-link.

@base <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eye/reasoning/issue141/test2.n3> .
@prefix : <http://www.example.com/ns/ex#> .

# Capture the property and its associated class in a new backward rule.
# The rule can answer a self-link question for any member of that class.
{
    ?p a :Reflexive .
    ?p :range-include ?C
} => {
    {
        ?x ?p ?x
    } <= {
        ?x a ?C
    } .
} .

# Enable the rule for like and Human; Socrates supplies a class member.
:like a :Reflexive ;
    :range-include :Human .
:Socrates a :Human .
